Change: Reject a user home that leaves the data directory through a symlink

verifyHomeLocation() checks the home path a user backend reports against the
configured datadirectory. It resolved the reported path with realpath(), which
returns false for a directory that does not exist yet - the normal case for a
user who has never logged in. Only the lexical form was checked then, and that
form cannot see a symlink in an intermediate segment of the path.

The longest existing prefix of the path is now resolved as well and must also
lie inside the data directory. A home below a symlink that points outside the
data directory is rejected before the home directory is created. A data
directory that is itself reached through a symlink keeps working as before.
